HTML DOM

Document Object Model
.structured representation of a web page 
.allows developers to access, modify, and control webpage content and structure using JS
.it powers most dynamic website interactions, enabling features like real-time updates, form validation, and interactive user interfaces 
.its a tree structure 
    .each HTML tag is a node 
    .<html> is the root element 
        .contains both <head> and <body> as child elements
.container elements - those nesting other elements 
.child elements - don't contain other elements 
.the hierarchy allows developers to navigate and manipulate web page content using JS 
    .by traversing from parent to child and vice versa 

Structure 
    .document  ==  root 
    .HTML tags == branches 
    .attributes, texts and other elements == leaves 


Requirement/ Need for DOM
.dynamic content updates 
    .allows content updates without reloading the page e.g form validation
.user interaction 
    .it makes the webpage interactive e.g responding to button clicks
.flexibility  
    .devs can add, modify, or remove elements and styles in real time 
.cross-platform compatibility 
    .provides standard way for scripts to interact with web documents, ensuring browser compatibility

Working of DOM
.it connects the webpage to JS, allowing me to:
    .access elements 
    .modify content 
    .react to event 
    .create or remove elements dynamically 

Types of DOM
.3 parts:
    .Core DOM
        .standard model for all document types 
    .XML DOM 
        .standard model for XML documents 
    .HTML DOM 
        .standard model for HTML documents     

Properties 
.node-based 
    .element nodes, text nodes, attribute nodes 
.hierarchical 
    .it has parent-child relationship forming tree structure 
.live 
    .changes made to the DOM using JS are immediately reflected on the web page 
.platform-independent 
    .it works across different platforms, browsers, and programming languages 

The Document 
.the document interface represents a web page loaded in the browser and acts as the main entry point to 
its content
.it allows devs to access and manipulate the page through the DOM tree
.the interface provides global access to page information such as the URL 
.it enables creating, modifying, and managing elements within the web page 


The Object
.all the properties, methods, and events available for manipulating and creating webpages are organized into 
objects inside DOM
.modern DOM id built using APIs working together 
.the core DOM defines the objects that fundamentally describe a document and the objects within it
.this is enhanced and expanded upon need
    e.g the HTML DOM API adds support for representing HTML documents to the core DOM 

The Interface
.an interface is like a blueprint that defines the properties and methods available for different types of elements
    e.g a <table> element uses the HTMLTableElement interface which gives it special table-specific methods 
.most elements inherit features from more general interfaces like Element and Node allowing devs to interact with 
them more easily using JS
    HTML Table Element => HTML Element => Document => Node => Event Target

    .shows how different types of HTML elements are related through interfaces:
        .EventTarget - base interface from which most DOM nodes inherit
            .allows elements to listen for and respond to events
        .Node - extends EventTarget and represents any single point in the document tree, such as elements, text
